 "notes": "Protocol pins: arms = exp79's plateau arms (scale_free, random3, torus; fixed labeling). Field kernel (zero-knob): w_ij = 1/r_ij^2 row-normalized, r_ij = Euclidean distance on the torus lattice coordinates where defined, else the graph-distance embedding (hop counts); Phi = weighted mean of the other cells' Vmem, term = kappa*(Phi - V) on dV only. F1's primary condition is the pre-named one with the unnamed dials left at the frozen defaults (gamma=0.25, mu=0.015 \u2014 the run_gm operating point; kappa=0 IS the frozen stack); the panel also records the kappa=0 control, the anchor-mu=0 variant and the star+field variant, plus the head-region errs, so the attribution is checkable either way. F2(a) is F1's verdict per the docstring ('F1's condition'); F2(b) re-asserts exp79's TC-G3 with its own seeds (1,2,3)+(4,5,6). F3's field-term: phi_ratio = kappa*f_wrong/(gamma + kappa) at the worst head cell, f_wrong = the row-normalized field weight on wrong-pattern cells \u2014 the structural analog of exp79's y. F4's primary noise convention is the house one-time V-noise (exp232's v_noise family): the write's initialization V-noise raised from sigma=2 to sigma=5 at matched (arm, gamma, mu, W=1, seeds); the sustained per-step variant is disclosed non-gating. Instrument: the kappa=0 FieldCollective path is asserted bit-exact against exp79's run_gm (the PD-G0 pattern) before any panel is trusted.",
 "finding": "F1 REFUTE: the head write at w=0 (exp79's head-shell protocol) + kappa=0.5 at the frozen defaults (g0.25/mu0.015, fresh seeds) errs 9.42-12.12 mV across the 3 plateau arms (0/3 under the 6.0 bar); the kappa=0 control already errs 3.34-7.75 (the mu=0.015 theta channel, whose diffusion rides the un-weighted topology and is NOT cut by the shell), and with the theta channel anchored (mu=0) the field's OWN drag at the frozen gamma still errs up to 10.62 \u2014 f_wrong 0.58-0.90 puts a 2/3-weighted trunk pull on every head cell, the field RE-INTRODUCES the cross-boundary hijack the shell cut removed; only the star gamma=64 dilutes the field-on write below the bar (0.12-0.21 mV); F2 REFUTE: (a)=F1 REFUTE, (b) the junction-only star (g64/mu0/kappa=0, TC-G3 re-asserted) holds at 0.57/0.57 PASS; F3 REFUTE: pred3=max(V,theta,field) over the 27-point (gamma x kappa) grid at mu=0.015 pools at Spearman 0.700 (exp79's own deposited 0.838) with 78% boundary agreement \u2014 the theta-term binds pred3 and is kappa-blind while the measured errs rise with kappa, and the field-term formula (CONTRAST*phi/(1+phi), phi=kappa*f/(gamma+kappa)) is the drag the max-form cannot add; the quadrature composition (disclosed, non-gating) pools at 0.933/78%; F4 REFUTE: under V-noise sigma=5 the kappa=0.5/kappa=0 write-err ratios are scale_free 1.05, random3 1.09, torus 1.25 \u2014 nowhere near the named 2x: the sigma=5 initialization transient decays to <0.3% inside the 24 t.u. window at both kappas (the ratios equal the no-noise drag ratios), and the sustained per-step disclosure shows the all-to-all field AVERAGING per-cell noise (differential fluctuations synchronize toward the weighted mean) instead of amplifying it \u2014 the named cost inverts in this stack."
